	(descr "KF128-5.08-2P 2-pos screw terminal, EDGE-TRIMMED for rf-de-20m. J101 is at board-local x = 3.70 rotated -90 so its wire-entry face hangs 1.6 mm off the board (HS-3 forces the THT pads clear of the heatsink land, LEARNINGS 2026-08-08), and the stock silk body outline, the two side-tab strokes, the pin-1 dot and the four wire-entry arrows all fell over air -> 6 silk_edge_clearance warnings. Every F.SilkS element with local y > 3.375 mm (= 0.2 mm clear of the board edge once half the 0.25 mm stroke is allowed for) is trimmed or dropped here. Nothing informative is lost: the removed marks are on the face that is not over laminate, and KiCad plots them nowhere. COPPER, DRILLS, PADS AND COURTYARD ARE UNTOUCHED - the courtyard still carries the real body extent.")
